<title>UK: Royal Dutch/Shell Q3 profits rise.</title>
<headline>Royal Dutch/Shell Q3 profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to Sept 30</p>
<p>		 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p>Current cost net income excluding special items</p>
<p>				1,117		  vs 1,202</p>
<p>Current cost net income including special items</p>
<p>				1,201		  vs 1,117</p>
<p> Net income		 1,329		  vs 1,053</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on current cost profits were in a range of 1.15 to 1.28 billion stg.  </p>
<p> Shr (guilders) Royal Dutch  4.13	     vs 3.16</p>
<p> Shr (pence) Shell Transport 14.5	     vs 11.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Royal Dutch/Shell Group is some 60 percent owned by Royal Dutch Petroleum Co of the Netherlands and 40 percent by Britain's Shell Transport and Trading Co Plc.</p>
<p> Net proceeds	     20,390		 vs 17,115</p>
<p> Gross profit	     4,533		  vs 3,694</p>
<p> Operating profit	 2,652		  vs 1,949</p>
<p> Interest income	  121		    vs 158</p>
<p> Interest expense	 152		    vs 191</p>
<p> Tax			  1,239		  vs 885</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN OF EARNINGS PER INDUSTRY SEGMENT -</p>
<p> Oil and gas		599		    vs 312</p>
<p> Refining and marketing 550		    vs 513</p>
<p> Chemicals		  273		    vs 317</p>
<p> Coal			 24		     vs 9</p>
<p> Other			6 deficit	    vs 29 deficit</p>
<p> Corporate items	  57 deficit	   vs 42 deficit</p>
<p> Minority interests     54 deficit	   vs 27 deficit</p>
<p>Equity crude oil production (thousand barrels per day)</p>
<p>				2,302		  vs 2,213</p>
<p>Natural gas sales (million cubic feet per day)</p>
<p>				6,839		  vs 6,221</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
